course: dictionary
lesson: 4811
title: One word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Attila led the Huns, horse-riding warriors from the east» is about history. The Huns were a people, so here hun is a name for a group of people.
explain: Now read «You OK, hun?» in a text message. Nobody is asking about a people from long ago. Hun is a friendly word here, like love or dear. The clues are the question and the kind of message it is.
explain: Some words are not kind to use. In old war stories, «the Hun» was an insulting name for German soldiers. Notice when a word is name-calling, and do not copy it. Asking "what would fit here?" helps you choose the right meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have more than one meaning: hun can be a people, and hun can also be a friendly word.
fact: The Huns were a nomadic people from Central Asia who rode into Europe in the 300s and 400s AD.
fact: In slang, especially in the UK and Australia, «hun» is a short form of «honey», used like «love» or «dear».
fact: «The Hun» was an offensive name in the First and Second World Wars, and it is not used for people today.
exercise: «Attila led the Huns, horse-riding warriors from the east.» In this sentence, what are the Huns? | *A people who rode into Europe long ago | A friendly word for a dear friend | A name for a shop | A kind of horse
exercise: «You OK, hun?» is sent in a text message. What does hun mean? | *A friendly word, like love or dear | A famous leader | A place in the mountains | A soldier from a war
exercise: Why should you notice when «the Hun» is used in an old war poster? | *It is an insulting name for German soldiers, so it shows hatred | It is a fun nickname to copy | It means the same as honey | It is a famous history fact to learn by heart
test: The word hun can be a people or a friendly word. What helps you choose the right meaning? | The colour of the page | The length of the word | *The words and sentence around it | Guessing from the first letter
test: Priya gets £2 back from Mia with "cheers, hun". What is hun doing in this message? | Telling Priya to hurry | Calling Mia a German soldier | *Showing friendly thanks, like dear | Naming a group of warriors
exam: In «Attila led the Huns, horse-riding warriors from the east», what does Huns mean? | A slang word for angry | *A nomadic people from Central Asia | A kind of petrol station | A friendly word for a friend
